(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[12 1 "// compile()'s PyCF_ONLY_AST (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200; ast.parse, ast.literal_eval): the host parses (the compiler's"] [13 1 "// mode \"ast:MODE:FLAGS:FEATURE:OPTIMIZE\"; since PY9, queue 201, the native reader, arbace.repr.python.astjson, in"] [14 1 "// tools/pyi/ast_json.py's form) and answers the tree as JSON; here it is rebuilt as the _ast module's nodes. A compile()"] [15 1 "// of an AST object is converted and validated first (queue 202c, builtins_ast_validate.go), then unparses it"] [16 1 "// (ast.unparse) and compiles the text: its positions are the unparsed text's."] [18 1 "// parseAST is the tree of source as _ast nodes."] [24 2 "// the compiler's answer for a SyntaxError (PY9: the native reader's, IndentationError and TabError too, the text"] [25 2 "// the parser's)"] [56 2 "// optimize > 0 or 2 (queue 202c): the tree preprocessed as ast_preprocess.c does (builtins_ast_opt.go)"] [126 1 "// astIntLiteralLimit is the parser's int digits limit (_PyPegen_number_token: PyLong_FromString's ValueError for a"] [127 1 "// decimal literal of more than sys.get_int_max_str_digits() digits, a SyntaxError of the literal's line, columns"] [128 1 "// 0). The host's parser does not know the runtime's limit and its answer gives the value in decimal, so the literal's"] [129 1 "// radix is read from the source at the node's position: a decimal literal has as many digits as its value, less"] [130 1 "// its underscores (queue 211: test_ast's test_literal_eval_str_int_limit)."] [163 1 "// astIdentifierKey is whether a field's values are identifiers (or lists of them), interned as the parser's"] [164 1 "// _PyPegen_new_identifier interns them (queue 202c: node.id is 'x')."] [239 1 "// unparseAST is ast.unparse(tree), for compile() of an AST object."] [245 2 "// __import__(\"ast\") is the package's top: ast itself"] [261 1 "// isASTNode is o an instance of _ast.AST."] [275 1 "// compile() of an AST object (queue 202c; Python/bltinmodule.c's is_ast branch): the object is converted as"] [276 1 "// Python-ast.c's obj2ast_* functions convert it (the node's fields and attributes by Parser/Python.asdl, TypeError and"] [277 1 "// ValueError as theirs), then checked by Python/ast.c's _PyAST_Validate. With PyCF_ONLY_AST the tree is preprocessed"] [278 1 "// (Python/ast_preprocess.c: optimize > 0's folding, optimize 2's docstrings) and made objects again as"] [279 1 "// PyAST_mod2obj makes them; else it is unparsed and the text compiled (PY6h's design)."] [281 1 "// astField is a field or an attribute of Python.asdl: its name, its type and its quantifier (\"\", \"?\", \"*\")."] [284 1 "// astCon is a constructor of a sum (sum its sum's name) or a product type (sum \"\")."] [291 1 "// astSum is a sum type: its attributes and constructors; simple when no constructor has a field."] [301 27 "// constructors of sums and products, by name"] [302 27 "// the _ast module's classes, by name"] [315 1 "// astSchemaOf is the schema of astTable with the module's classes (the module imported first)."] [357 1 "// astNode is a node of the C level's tree: its constructor's (or product's) name and its fields' values: nil (NULL),"] [358 1 "// *astNode, []any (a sequence), Object (identifier, string, constant) or int; pos its attributes when it has some."] [396 1 "// obj2ast converts obj, a value of the asdl type typ (obj2ast_TYPE)."] [458 1 "// field converts the field f of obj for owner (the node's name in the messages)."] [503 1 "// attrs reads the position attributes (the optional ends default to the starts)."] [532 1 "// fields reads a constructor's fields, then checks its required ones as the C constructor (_PyAST_NAME) does."] [612 1 "// astObj2Mod is PyAST_obj2mod: the mode's node checked (PyAst_CheckMode), then converted."] [634 1 "// ---- Python/ast.c: _PyAST_Validate ----"] [1377 1 "// astValidate is _PyAST_Validate."] [1394 1 "// ---- PyAST_mod2obj ----"] [1396 1 "// ast2obj makes x, a value of the asdl type typ, objects again (ast2obj_TYPE): a node of the _ast module's class with"] [1397 1 "// every field and attribute set."] [1439 1 "// compileASTObject is compile()'s branch for an AST object: with PyCF_ONLY_AST the converted, validated and"] [1440 1 "// preprocessed tree as objects; else the validated tree's text (ast.unparse) for the compiler."] [1460 1 "// The AST's preprocessing (queue 202c; Python/ast_preprocess.c, _PyAST_Preprocess, as compile() runs it for"] [1461 1 "// PyCF_ONLY_AST): with PyCF_OPTIMIZED_AST (ast.parse's optimize > 0) the folding: __debug__ a constant, a str's %"] [1462 1 "// formatting with a tuple a JoinedStr, a pattern's negative and complex numbers constants; with optimize 2 the"] [1463 1 "// docstrings removed. Without PyCF_OPTIMIZED_AST (syntax_check_only) only the docstrings at optimize 2."] [1473 1 "// astNeedsPreprocess is whether the preprocessing can change a tree."] [1478 1 "// astPreprocess is _PyCompile_AstPreprocess (its future features from the tree, _PyFuture_FromAST)."] [1499 1 "// astFutureAnnotations is `from __future__ import annotations` among the module's leading statements (future.c)."] [1527 1 "// astDocString is _PyAST_GetDocString: the body's first statement's str constant."] [1763 1 "// astMakeConst makes e the constant v (make_const), its position kept."] [1788 1 "// astOptimizeFormat is optimize_format: '%s %r' % (a, b) as an f-string, when every unit is a simple s, r or a."] [1793 3 "// parse_literal"] [1834 1 "// astParseFormat is parse_format with simple_format_arg_parse (at most two digits of width and of precision)."] [1920 1 "// foldMatchConst is fold_const_match_patterns: -C and C1 +/- C2 of a pattern's value made constants."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[45 26] [61 53] [92 32] [97 49] [136 30] [154 32] [179 24] [188 52] [387 23] [390 47] [427 28] [441 27] [444 25] [480 13] [480 20] [485 31] [515 22] [545 31] [571 48] [581 44] [601 44] [671 46] [674 43] [677 49] [686 55] [696 28] [699 33] [